# explicit call-site type-args (fn/method) — aditivo, colheita à mão (2026-08-11)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generics could be DECLARED (`fn id<T>`, `Box<T>`) and CALLED only with `T` INFERRED from the
# arguments. The owner ruled that if generics exist, they must be instantiable EXPLICITLY at the call
# site — for both a free FUNCTION and an instance METHOD. This reseed carries that feature, purely
# ADDITIVE over the corpus (nothing in the tree writes the new spelling, so every existing call is
# byte-identical). What landed:
#   - PARSER. `MethodCall` gained a `type_args: []TypeExpr` field. `parse_postfix` grows a speculative
#     `recv.m<T>(args)` branch, and `parse_atom` a speculative `foo<T>(args)` / `ns::foo<T>(args)`
#     branch. Both reuse `parse_type_args` + backtrack: a `<…>` list only commits when it CLOSES
#     (`pending_gt == 0`) AND a `(` follows — otherwise it backtracks to a comparison, so `a < b` and
#     the chain `a < b < c` are untouched. The `(`-commit is NOT struct-gated (unambiguous once the
#     `(` is seen), so an explicit call works inside an if/match scrutinee too; the `{` (typed struct
#     literal) and `::` (generic static call) commits stay struct-gated exactly as before.
#   - CHECKER. `type_call` disambiguates the two shapes that share the `Call` node — a generic STATIC
#     call `Type<Args>::m(…)` (args bind the OWNER TYPE, retargeted as before) vs an explicit
#     FUNCTION/METHOD call (args bind the FUNCTION's own type-params) — by resolving the callee. When
#     explicit args are present they WIN over inference: the signature's type-params bind to the given
#     types (in appearance order), the typed args must fit the substituted parameters, and a type-param
#     that appears ONLY in the return type (uninferable from args) becomes callable. `type_method_call`
#     threads `mc.type_args` through its desugar into `type_call`.
#   - MONOMORPH. `TCall` gained `type_args: []Type` (the RESOLVED explicit args). The mono pass, at a
#     generic-fn call carrying them, binds the instance Subst from the explicit args (substituted
#     through the enclosing instantiation) INSTEAD of re-inferring from the argument types — so the
#     stamped instance matches what the typer chose (explicit wins end-to-end). A bare/inferred call
#     keeps the pre-existing inference path, byte-identical.
#   - .tkb. The typed-tree codec appends `TCall.type_args` (a type list, empty for every bare call) on
#     the plain-call tag, defaulting to empty on read — format stays append/compatible, no ordinal
#     broke.
# Proven by a probe (examples/probes/explicit_type_args): `id<i64>(3)`, `first<A,B>`, the return-only
# `empty_list<i64>()`, and the method `b.wrap<i64>(9)` all PARSE + CHECK + LOWER + run (exit 0); the
# bare `empty_list()` still errors "cannot infer … only in the return type". Comparisons and the whole
# generic corpus (examples/regressions/own_native) are byte-identical in behavior.
